# Frontend architecture

Organize by feature. Keep technical folders inside the feature that owns them.

```text
src/
  app/                      router, providers, app shell
  features/<feature>/
    components/
    hooks/
    services/
    model/                  types and pure business rules
    index.ts                public exports only
  shared/
    ui/                     components used by more than one feature
    lib/                    pure helpers with no feature knowledge
```

- Components render. Hooks own state and effects. Services perform I/O. `model/` holds rules that stay valid without React.
- Pages compose features. They do not encode pricing, eligibility, or listing rules.
- A feature may import `shared/` and its own files. It must not import another feature's internals. Cross-feature use goes through that feature's `index.ts`.
- Move a component to `shared/ui` only after a second feature needs it.
- Keep route modules thin: load data, call a feature hook or service, then render.
